<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds closed on Wednesday, reopen May 1.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds closed on Wednesday, reopen May 1.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch bond market is closed on Wednesday for the Koninginnedag (Queen's Day) national holiday and will reopen on Thursday, May 1.</p>
<p>Bonds closed sharply higher on Tuesday ahead of the holiday, with the 10-year 5.75 percent 2007 benchmark bond up 0.52 points to 100.08/16 for a 5.73 percent bid yield.</p>
<p>----Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 570 8500</p>
